Stage-05 lifecycle audit — SIGTERM drain and SIGHUP reload
Harness: local socket upstream, upstream delay as noted, one client request issued,
SIGTERM delivered at t+0.3 s. Every command wrapped in `timeout`.
Spec: stages/capabilities/operations.md:6-7
  "On SIGHUP reread the entire configuration atomically. An invalid reload retains the
   previous configuration. ... On SIGTERM stop accepting new connections, finish in-flight
   responses up to drain_timeout_ms, then exit."
=====================================================================

A. DRAIN, upstream delay 5.0 s, drain_timeout_ms 2000
   build     body_delivered  client_closed  master
   e1a28e35  0/10            +2.01s         exited +2.11s      deadline honoured, body lost
   afdc173f  0/10            +2.01s         exited +2.11s      deadline honoured, body lost
   f2b3415b  0/10            +2.01s         exited +2.11s      deadline honoured, body lost
   6baf167b  0/10            NEVER          NEVER_EXITED (also at 30 s)  *** hard hang
   ae021893  0/10            NEVER          NEVER_EXITED (also at 30 s)  *** hard hang
   Reproduced 3/3 for 6baf167b and ae021893, 2/2 for the other three.

B. IDLE SERVER, drain_timeout_ms 500, observation 30 s
   6baf167b  NEVER_EXITED after 30.0 s
   ae021893  NEVER_EXITED after 30.0 s
   e1a28e35  exited +0.50 s  (correct)
   So the hang does not need traffic at all.

C. WHY THE HANG — thread parking at the exit path (6baf167b)
   `worker()` is `for(;;)` with no exit condition:
     line 102  static void worker(){UpConn pool;for(;;){Task task;{unique_lock<mutex>g(qm);
               qcv.wait(g,[]{return !queuework.empty();});...}}
   the pool is started once, detached:
     line 110  ...i<workers...i++)thread(worker).detach()
   The main loop breaks correctly on the deadline:
     line 110  }if(draining&&(clients.empty()||Clock::now()>=drainend))break
   but process exit then has to tear down the live threads, which are parked in
   `futex_do_wait` inside the condition-variable wait and are never signalled.
   /proc observation 2 s after SIGTERM (ev_s5_hang_threads.log): 33 threads, every one in
   state S with wchan futex_do_wait, main thread included; listener fd already closed so the
   broker really did reach its exit path.

D. THE MEASURED SOCIAL COST (6baf167b, 5 s upstream delay, drain 1000 ms)
   at +2.5 s: master alive, fds 7, 2 sockets, 1 upstream accept, client path OPEN
   client read: TimeoutError at +32.6 s — no EOF, no bytes, ever
   So a stopped-but-hanging instance holds the client socket and the upstream socket open
   indefinitely while giving the client no signal at all.

E. RELOAD (SIGHUP) — correctness baseline is good
   e1a28e35 / 6baf167b / afdc173f / ae021893 / f2b3415b (cache on for f2b3415b):
     before=ALPHA after=BETA reloaded=YES master_alive=True
   All five switch the root on SIGHUP while the master survives, satisfying
   operations.md:6.  No reload defect found on stage-05.

F. FILES THAT MUST BE PRESENT (so a replay with a short config starts)
   All keys are mandatory (INTERFACE.md: "All keys listed in the stage configuration are
   required"); additionally host_root, alias and redirect must all be present and resolvable,
   and f2b3415b requires cache_ttl_ms/cache_bytes non-zero and an exact key set.
